  "rule": "A full-span wall has jagged long edges (notches and bumps). Each loose single-colour piece is translated, without rotation or flipping, so that it locks into the wall. One notch seeds a chain of same-width pieces. Each piece's near profile exactly complements the current edge in every column. The chain stops when the outer edge becomes straight. All pieces are used once, and the wall and its decoy notches stay unchanged.",
  "scope": "Supported: native grid width 18..30 along the wall and height 22..30. The wall can be horizontal or transposed to vertical, with random wall colour and thickness 5..7. Notch depths are 1..2 and bumps are 1 cell on both edges, with random decoy notches and bumps. There are 1..3 chains of distinct widths 3..6 on either side, with 1..3 pieces each. Cut profiles between pieces are random but stay 4-connected. Piece colours are random and differ from the wall colour; neighbouring pieces in a chain have different colours, and colours may repeat across a chain. Input positions are scattered anywhere in the free space. Not supported: background colours other than 0; two chains sharing a width; chains whose pieces have different widths; hollow or non-tiling chains; rotated or reflected pieces; walls that do not span the grid. Fixtures are rebuilt from explicit latent arguments (wall profiles, chain cut profiles, colours and input positions).",
  "constraints": [
    "Background is 0; the wall is one 4-connected object spanning the full native width. The band is at least 5 thick and notches are at most 2 deep per side, so a solid core row always survives.",
    "Every piece is 4-connected, single-coloured, never the wall colour, and has at least one cell in every column of its chain.",
    "A chain's seed segment on the wall is non-flat with at least one notch. Intermediate cut profiles are non-flat, and only the last piece's outer edge is flat.",
    "Chains occupy disjoint column ranges separated by at least 2 columns. The columns next to a chain on its side are kept flat, so decoys never touch a chain notch.",
    "Finished chains and wall bumps stay inside the grid. The wall top is at least row 1 and the wall bottom is at most row height-2.",
    "Input pieces never touch the wall or each other, including diagonally, so the object segmentation is unambiguous. The input therefore always differs from the output.",
    "An ambiguity guard enumerates jigsaw chains for each width group from every non-flat wall window. A scene is accepted only if the intended placement is the unique cover. This rules out identical-shape swaps and decoy fits."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "The ambiguity guard re-implements jigsaw chain enumeration to reject ambiguous scenes. It only filters scenes; outputs always come from the latent placement.",
    "Only one chain per width is generated. The original task allows several chains of the same width in principle, but its fixtures do not need this.",
    "Background is fixed at 0 and the grid is at most 30x30. The canonical fixtures are all 30x30.",
    "Random scenes do not reproduce the exact piece vocabulary of the originals, such as specific staircase or triangle motifs. Shapes come from random cut profiles.",
    "Partial explicit geometry without chains is rejected. Width/height specify the native horizontal-wall frame; vertical=True transposes those dimensions."
  ],
